Work in progress

Automation framework using Page Object Model (POM) and Gherkin syntax with Pytest-BDD

Steps to run:
py -3.14 -m venv venv
.\venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1
pip install -r requirements.txt
pytest -s -v --platform android         # Android
pytest -s -v --platform ios             # iOS

The --platform flag (default: android) selects which mobile target the
Appium driver session runs against. Capabilities live in
config/capabilities.yaml; page objects per platform live under
pages/mobile/<platform>/. To add iOS, implement pages/mobile/ios/*.py and
register the classes in pages/mobile/pages.py under PAGE_CLASSES["iOS"].

Need Appium server and a device emulator.
Feature files live under tests/features/.
